//! MUST NOT COMPILE.
//!
//! `BeaconBlockBody` has 11 fields in Capella. Asking for field 12 of it is a
//! layout error; in Solidity it would be a gindex constant that is simply
//! wrong, and the mistake would survive until a proof was verified on chain.
//! Here `field_gindex` checks the position against the field count while the
//! constant is being evaluated, so the build stops.

use verife::gindex::field_gindex

const CAPELLA_BODY_FIELDS: u64 = 11

const OUT_OF_RANGE: u64 = field_gindex(field: 12, field_count: CAPELLA_BODY_FIELDS)

static_assert(OUT_OF_RANGE > 0)
